  "description": "BOYRIT crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C130 H166 Dy10 N44 Na2 O60 6+,2(C4 H10 O1),6(N1 O3 1-),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 13 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.661-4.216 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.75-123.51°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy10Na2L4(μ3-OH)4(DMF)12(NO3)6]·6NO3·2DMF·(CH3CH2)2O·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
